{
  "_comment": [
    "Provenance for the character master artwork.",
    "",
    "The masters are 80-210 MB each (~1.3 GB total) and are deliberately NOT in the",
    "repository: `assets/sources/characters/*.png` is gitignored. This manifest is",
    "what makes them recoverable without archaeology through git history \u2014 re-fetch",
    "by driveId, check the sha256, then run scripts/import-character-assets.py.",
    "",
    "`employee` is the authoritative link. Asset files are never matched to animals",
    "by filename: every entry names the employee id from src/content/employees.ts and",
    "the species recorded in src/art/critterShapes.ts, and a test asserts the two",
    "agree so a cat can never end up wearing the owl's artwork.",
    "",
    "`officeHeight` is the authored CSS height for that animal in the office diorama",
    "BEFORE the global presence multiplier in src/content/characterScale.ts.",
    "",
    "NOTE: this importer encodes @1x at `officeHeight`, which is NOT the size the",
    "sprite is drawn at -- the presence multiplier makes that officeHeight * 1.2. A",
    "fresh import therefore lands 20% short and reads soft; run",
    "scripts/reencode-cast-display-size.py afterwards to bring @1x up to the real",
    "display height. See docs/CHARACTER_SPRITE_SHARPNESS.md."
  ],
  "fetch": {
    "urlTemplate": "https://drive.usercontent.google.com/download?id={driveId}&export=download&confirm=t",
    "note": "Large files may be throttled; retry until the payload starts with the PNG signature and ends with IEND."
  },
